{"id":"mahabharata-3-177","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":177,"title":"सप्तसप्तत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 177 · Nahusha questions Yudhishthira","summary":{"en":"Nahusha asks Yudhishthira who is a Brahmin and what is to be known. Yudhishthira answers that a Brahmin is known by truth, generosity, forbearance and austerity, not birth alone, and that the supreme Brahman, beyond joy and sorrow, is what must be known; Nahusha agrees to release Bhima.","kn":"ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣನಾರು, ತಿಳಿಯಬೇಕಾದ್ದೇನು ಎಂದು ನಹುಷನು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನನ್ನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಜನ್ಮದಿಂದ ಮಾತ್ರವಲ್ಲ ಸತ್ಯ, ದಾನ, ಕ್ಷಮೆ, ತಪಸ್ಸಿನಿಂದ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣನು ತಿಳಿಯಲ್ಪಡುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಸುಖದುಃಖಾತೀತ ಪರಬ್ರಹ್ಮವೇ ತಿಳಿಯಬೇಕಾದ್ದು ಎಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಉತ್ತರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭೀಮನನ್ನು ಬಿಡಲು ನಹುಷನು ಒಪ್ಪುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"नहुष युधिष्ठिर से पूछते हैं कि ब्राह्मण कौन है और जानने योग्य क्या है। युधिष्ठिर उत्तर देते हैं कि ब्राह्मण केवल जन्म से नहीं, सत्य, दान, क्षमा और तप से पहचाना जाता है, और सुख-दुःख से परे परब्रह्म ही जानने योग्य है; नहुष भीम को छोड़ने को मान जाते हैं।","te":"బ్రాహ్మణుడెవరు, తెలుసుకోవలసినది ఏమిటని నహుషుడు యుధిష్ఠిరుని అడుగుతాడు. జన్మతోనే కాక సత్యం, దానం, క్షమ, తపస్సుతో బ్రాహ్మణుడు గుర్తించబడతాడని, సుఖదుఃఖాలకు అతీతమైన పరబ్రహ్మమే తెలుసుకోవలసినదని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు బదులిస్తాడు; భీముని విడిచిపెట్టడానికి నహుషుడు అంగీకరిస్తాడు.","ta":"அந்தணன் யார், அறிய வேண்டியது எது என்று நஹுஷன் யுதிஷ்டிரரிடம் கேட்கிறான். பிறப்பால் மட்டுமல்ல, உண்மை, கொடை, பொறுமை, தவம் ஆகியவற்றால் அந்தணன் அறியப்படுகிறான், இன்ப துன்பம் கடந்த பரப்ரஹ்மமே அறிய வேண்டியது என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் பதில் சொல்ல, பீமனை விடுவிக்க நஹுஷன் இசைகிறான்.","ml":"ബ്രാഹ്മണൻ ആരാണെന്നും അറിയേണ്ടത് എന്താണെന്നും നഹുഷൻ യുധിഷ്ഠിരനോട് ചോദിക്കുന്നു. സത്യം, ദാനം, ക്ഷമ, തപസ്സ് എന്നിവകൊണ്ടാണ് ബ്രാഹ്മണനെ അറിയുന്നത്, ജന്മംകൊണ്ടല്ലെന്നും; സുഖദുഃഖങ്ങൾക്ക് അതീതമായ പരബ്രഹ്മമാണ് അറിയേണ്ടതെന്നും യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ മറുപടി നൽകുന്നു; ഭീമനെ വിട്ടയക്കാമെന്ന് നഹുഷൻ സമ്മതിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.177; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"आजगरपर्व","titleEn":"Ajagara Parva (The python)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"युधिष्ठिरस्तमासाद्य सर्पभोगाभिवेष्टितम् ।\nदयितं भ्रातरं वीरमिदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Coming up to his dear brother, the hero, wrapped in the serpent's coils, Yudhishthira spoke these words."}},{"n":2,"text":"कुन्तीमातः कथमिमामापदं त्वमवाप्तवान् ।\nकश्चायं पर्वताभोगप्रतिमः पन्नगोत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Son of Kunti, how have you fallen into this calamity? And who is this best of serpents, like a mountain mass?\""}},{"n":3,"text":"स धर्मराजमालक्ष्य भ्राता भ्रातरमग्रजम् ।\nकथयामास तत्सर्वं ग्रहणादि विचेष्टितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the king of dharma, his elder brother, Bhima told him everything, beginning with how he was seized and all that he did."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"देवो वा यदि वा दैत्य उरगो वा भवान्यदि ।\nसत्यं सर्प वचो ब्रूहि पृच्छति त्वां युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Whether you are a god, a daitya or a serpent, speak the truth, serpent. Yudhishthira asks you."}},{"n":5,"text":"किमाहृत्य विदित्वा वा प्रीतिस्ते स्याद्भुजंगम ।\nकिमाहारं प्रयच्छामि कथं मुञ्चेद्भवानिमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What would please you, serpent, to bring or to know? What food shall I give you, or how might you release him?\""}},{"text":"सर्प उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The serpent said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"नहुषो नाम राजाहमासं पूर्वस्तवानघ ।\nप्रथितः पञ्चमः सोमादायोः पुत्रो नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Sinless one, I was Nahusha, a king, your ancestor, famed as the fifth from Soma, the son of Ayu, lord of men."}},{"n":7,"text":"क्रतुभिस्तपसा चैव स्वाध्यायेन दमेन च ।\nत्रैलोक्यैश्वर्यमव्यग्रं प्राप्तो विक्रमणेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"By sacrifices, austerity, study and self-control, and by my valor, I attained undisturbed lordship over the three worlds."}},{"n":8,"text":"तदैश्वर्यं समासाद्य दर्पो मामगमत्तदा ।\nसहस्रं हि द्विजातीनामुवाह शिबिकां मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"When I had that sovereignty, pride took hold of me, and a thousand brahmins carried my palanquin."}},{"n":9,"text":"ऐश्वर्यमदमत्तोऽहमवमन्य ततो द्विजान् ।\nइमामगस्त्येन दशामानीतः पृथिवीपते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drunk with the pride of power, I then scorned the brahmins, and Agastya brought me to this state, lord of the earth."}},{"n":10,"text":"न तु मामजहात्प्रज्ञा यावदद्येति पाण्डव ।\nतस्यैवानुग्रहाद्राजन्नगस्त्यस्य महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But my understanding has not left me even today, Pandava, by the grace of that great-souled Agastya, O king."}},{"n":11,"text":"षष्ठे काले ममाहारः प्राप्तोऽयमनुजस्तव ।\nनाहमेनं विमोक्ष्यामि न चान्यमभिकामये ॥","meaning":{"en":"This younger brother of yours has come to me as food at the sixth part of the day. I will not release him, and I desire no other."}},{"n":12,"text":"प्रश्नानुच्चारितांस्तु त्वं व्याहरिष्यसि चेन्मम ।\nअथ पश्चाद्विमोक्ष्यामि भ्रातरं ते वृकोदरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But if you answer the questions I put, I will release your brother Vrikodara afterward.\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"ब्रूहि सर्प यथाकामं प्रतिवक्ष्यामि ते वचः ।\nअपि चेच्छक्नुयां प्रीतिमाहर्तुं ते भुजंगम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Ask, serpent, as you please. I will answer your words, and I will try to bring you pleasure, serpent."}},{"n":14,"text":"वेद्यं यद्ब्राह्मणेनेह तद्भवान्वेत्ति केवलम् ।\nसर्पराज ततः श्रुत्वा प्रतिवक्ष्यामि ते वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You alone know what a brahmin should know here. Having heard from you, king of serpents, I will answer.\""}},{"text":"सर्प उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The serpent said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"ब्राह्मणः को भवेद्राजन्वेद्यं किं च युधिष्ठिर ।\nब्रवीह्यतिमतिं त्वां हि वाक्यैरनुमिमीमहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Who is a brahmin, O king, and what is to be known, Yudhishthira? Tell me, for by your words we judge you of high intelligence.\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"सत्यं दानं क्षमा शीलमानृशंस्यं दमो घृणा ।\nदृश्यन्ते यत्र नागेन्द्र स ब्राह्मण इति स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Where truth, charity, forbearance, good conduct, kindness, self-control and compassion are seen, king of serpents, that person is said to be a brahmin."}},{"n":17,"text":"वेद्यं सर्प परं ब्रह्म निर्दुःखमसुखं च यत् ।\nयत्र गत्वा न शोचन्ति भवतः किं विवक्षितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What is to be known, serpent, is the supreme Brahman, which is free of pain and of pleasure, and those who reach it grieve no more. What more do you wish to say?\""}},{"text":"सर्प उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The serpent said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"चातुर्वर्ण्यं प्रमाणं च सत्यं च ब्रह्म चैव ह ।\nशूद्रेष्वपि च सत्यं च दानमक्रोध एव च ।\nआनृशंस्यमहिंसा च घृणा चैव युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The fourfold order is authoritative, and truth and Brahman too. Truth, charity, freedom from anger, kindness, non-violence and compassion are found even among shudras, Yudhishthira."}},{"n":19,"text":"वेद्यं यच्चात्थ निर्दुःखमसुखं च नराधिप ।\nताभ्यां हीनं पदं चान्यन्न तदस्तीति लक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"And as for what you say is to be known, free of pain and pleasure, lord of men, I do not see that any state exists which is free of both of those.\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"शूद्रे चैतद्भवेल्लक्ष्यं द्विजे तच्च न विद्यते ।\nन वै शूद्रो भवेच्छूद्रो ब्राह्मणो न च ब्राह्मणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If these marks are found in a shudra and are not found in a twice-born, then the shudra is not a shudra and the brahmin is not a brahmin."}},{"n":21,"text":"यत्रैतल्लक्ष्यते सर्प वृत्तं स ब्राह्मणः स्मृतः ।\nयत्रैतन्न भवेत्सर्प तं शूद्रमिति निर्दिशेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where this conduct is seen, serpent, that person is said to be a brahmin; where it is not, serpent, one should call him a shudra."}},{"n":22,"text":"यत्पुनर्भवता प्रोक्तं न वेद्यं विद्यतेति ह ।\nताभ्यां हीनमतीत्यात्र पदं नास्तीति चेदपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"And as for what you said, that there is nothing to be known, since no state exists beyond and free of those two, even that, serpent, is my view too."}},{"n":23,"text":"एवमेतन्मतं सर्प ताभ्यां हीनं न विद्यते ।\nयथा शीतोष्णयोर्मध्ये भवेन्नोष्णं न शीतता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Such a state free of both does not exist as in the middle between heat and cold there is neither heat nor cold."}},{"n":24,"text":"एवं वै सुखदुःखाभ्यां हीनमस्ति पदं क्वचित् ।\nएषा मम मतिः सर्प यथा वा मन्यते भवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the same way, there is somewhere a state free of pleasure and pain. This is my view, serpent, or as you think.\""}},{"text":"सर्प उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The serpent said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"यदि ते वृत्ततो राजन्ब्राह्मणः प्रसमीक्षितः ।\nव्यर्था जातिस्तदायुष्मन्कृतिर्यावन्न दृश्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If a brahmin is to be judged by conduct, O king, then birth is useless, long-lived one, so long as the conduct is not seen.\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"जातिरत्र महासर्प मनुष्यत्वे महामते ।\nसंकरात्सर्ववर्णानां दुष्परीक्ष्येति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Birth among human beings, great serpent and wise one, is hard to judge, I think, because of the mixing of all the classes."}},{"n":27,"text":"सर्वे सर्वास्वपत्यानि जनयन्ति यदा नराः ।\nवाङ्मैथुनमथो जन्म मरणं च समं नृणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All men beget children on all women; speech, mating, birth and death are the same for all men."}},{"n":28,"text":"इदमार्षं प्रमाणं च ये यजामह इत्यपि ।\nतस्माच्छीलं प्रधानेष्टं विदुर्ये तत्त्वदर्शिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is also the authority of the sages, who say, 'What do we sacrifice?' Therefore those who see the truth hold that good conduct is the chief concern."}},{"n":29,"text":"प्राङ्नाभिवर्धनात्पुंसो जातकर्म विधीयते ।\nतत्रास्य माता सावित्री पिता त्वाचार्य उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The birth rite of a man is laid down before the cutting of the navel cord; at that time his mother is Savitri and his father is called the teacher."}},{"n":30,"text":"वृत्त्या शूद्रसमो ह्येष यावद्वेदे न जायते ।\nअस्मिन्नेवं मतिद्वैधे मनुः स्वायम्भुवोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By conduct he is equal to a shudra until he is born in the Veda. In this conflict of opinion, Manu Svayambhuva has said it."}},{"n":31,"text":"कृतकृत्याः पुनर्वर्णा यदि वृत्तं न विद्यते ।\nसंकरस्तत्र नागेन्द्र बलवान्प्रसमीक्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If conduct is lacking, the classes have, so to speak, done their work, and mixing of classes is seen to be strong there, king of serpents."}},{"n":32,"text":"यत्रेदानीं महासर्प संस्कृतं वृत्तमिष्यते ।\nतं ब्राह्मणमहं पूर्वमुक्तवान्भुजगोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where, great serpent, refined conduct is now seen, I have already called that person a brahmin, best of serpents.\""}},{"text":"सर्प उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The serpent said:"}},{"n":33,"text":"श्रुतं विदितवेद्यस्य तव वाक्यं युधिष्ठिर ।\nभक्षयेयमहं कस्माद्भ्रातरं ते वृकोदरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Yudhishthira, I have heard your words, you who know what is to be known. Why then should I eat your brother Vrikodara?\""}}]}]}